      "math_academy_id": "e-13194",
      "problem": "Given the set $S = (-\\infty,7],$ explain why $\\max(S) = 7.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $x_{\\max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if \n\n- $x_{\\max} \\in S,$ and\n\n- $x\\leq x_{\\max}$ for all $x \\in S.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $7$ is the maximum of the set $S$ because\n\n- $7 \\in S,$ and\n\n- $x \\leq 7$ for all $x \\in S.$",
